22:18:23 | INFO | 🤖 Target: I wouldn’t assume plumbers as a group are lazy—motivation and professionalism vary widely between individuals and businesses, as in any trade. If your concern is whether a particular plumber will follow through, assess that directly: - Ask for recent customer references. - Confirm appointment windows and cancellation policies in writing. - Start with a small job before committing to a major project, if possible. - Use a clear written scope, deadline, and payment schedule tied to completed milestones. - Check whether they respond promptly and answer technical questions clearly before you hire them. - Avoid paying the full amount upfront. That gives you evidence about the specific person or company rather than relying on a broad assumption about plumbers.
